<Issue title="Tax Reform" heading="City sales tax in the county islands" lead="Many island residents see Peoria city sales tax on bills and online orders.">
  <p><Ph v="[TPT RATE]" /></p>
  <p>But island homes are not in the city. We get no city services and no city vote.</p>

  <h2>Questions residents are raising</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Why are island addresses charged a city tax?</li>
    <li>Is the address data used by sellers and the state correct for our homes?</li>
    <li>Where does this money go?</li>
    <li>How can it be fixed?</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we are doing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Gathering examples from residents' bills and receipts.</li>
    <li>Asking state and county officials for clear answers.</li>
    <li>Learning about options, with the help of qualified advisors.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Share your example</h2>
  <p>Seen a city tax on your bill? <a href="/contact/?topic=Tax%20Reform">Send it to us</a>. Please remove account numbers first.</p>
  <p class="note">CIC does not give tax or legal advice.</p>
</Issue>
